[[ values.description ]]

Technology: **[[ values.stack | default("nestjs") ]]**. Owner: `[[ values.owner ]]`.
Platform request: `[[ values.request_id ]]`.

The orchestrator adds this starter after infrastructure approval. Once its application PR merges,
developers can check out `https://github.com/[[ values.org ]]/[[ values.repo ]]` and run
`docker compose up --build -d`. The local service listens on `http://localhost:3000`.

- `/health/live` and `/health/ready`: process and readiness endpoints.
- `/v1/orders`: read-only sample orders, with no external database or credentials.
- `/docs`: API documentation or starter endpoint documentation.
- Frontend stacks also serve the sample page at `/`.

Replace the demo with application-specific logic. The new starters currently support runtime
capability **None** only; Azure Storage / Key Vault application integrations require implementation
before enabling those selections. Platform secrets remain managed by Azure Key Vault.

The generated Dockerfile is also used by CI and AKS deployment. All stacks use port 3000 and the
same Helm health contract. `APP_PORT`, `APP_MEMORY` and `APP_CPUS` adjust local Compose settings.
Memory ceilings are provisional; these starters have not been built, tested or deployed.

`infra/terraform` contains infrastructure, `deploy/helm/application` contains deployment values,
and `.github/workflows` calls the reviewed platform workflows. Dependency lockfiles and base-image
digests must be validated before release. Keep credentials out of Git and Docker build contexts.
